    <value>Quick Introduction Guide</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TextoManualCompleto" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Step 1: Select a Concept
• a) If the concept is already filtered in the accounting entries, it will appear selected by default.
• b) Expand the list using the arrow and select the desired one with the mouse.
• c) Click on the field and type the first letter: each press will cycle through the concepts starting with that letter. Press Enter when the desired one is selected.
Step 2: Enter a Description
• a) Leave the default description of the selected concept and press Enter to jump directly to the Amount.
• b) Add text to the generic description: if the text exists in the history, the search box will open with matches. Press the Down Arrow to navigate the list, select the desired one, and press Enter.
• c) Select all text, press Delete, and type at least 3 letters to open the search box. Navigate with the Down Arrow, select the desired option, and press Enter.
• d) For a new description, type the desired text and press Enter. The system will ask for confirmation to add it; confirm by pressing Yes.
Step 3: Enter the Amount
• Enter the amount and press Enter.
Step 4: Select the Bank Account
• a) If the bank account is already filtered in the accounting entries, it will appear selected by default.
• b) Expand the list using the arrow and select the desired one with the mouse.
• c) Click on the field and type the first letter: each press will cycle through the accounts starting with that letter. Press Enter when the desired one is selected.
Step 5: Finalize the Entry
• a) Enter a Note, if necessary.
• b) Press Accept and Next to keep entering transactions, or Accept and Exit to finish.</value>
